BT /F1 11 Tf 54 514 Td (2. start the split web stack,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 498 Td (3. upload a short English video,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 482 Td (4. run translation to Chinese,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 466 Td (5. review the final dubbed result and history replay.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 54 434 Td (8. Innovation and Practical Value) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 386 Td (This project focuses on practical multimodal creation rather than a toy demo. The main) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 370 Td (value lies in integrating several AI capabilities into a single creator-facing workflow:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 338 Td (- speech recognition,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 322 Td (- translation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 306 Td (- voice cloning,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 290 Td (- synchronized audio reconstruction,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 274 Td (- and deliverable video rendering.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 242 Td (The work is especially relevant for bilingual content creation and developer education,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 226 Td (where the ability to turn one source video into multiple localized versions has direct) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 210 Td (productivity value.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 54 178 Td (9. Current Limitations) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 130 Td (- The best current path is short-form, single-speaker content.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 114 Td (- Very long uploads may require proxy timeout tuning in some deployment setups.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 98 Td (- Multi-speaker support exists but is not the strongest demonstration path in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 82 Td (  current branch.) Tj ET
